msgstr "Mudanças incompatíveis na API"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:106
msgid ""
"User-visible API breaks between v3.8.0 and v3.9.0. Scope: Python C-modules "
"in ``modules/`` and Python libraries in ``scripts/libraries/``."
msgstr ""
"Quebras de API visíveis ao usuário entre a v3.8.0 e a v3.9.0. Escopo: "
"módulos C do Python em ``modules/`` e bibliotecas Python em "
"``scripts/libraries/``\\ ."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:109
msgid "Each change is tagged with its impact:"
msgstr "Cada mudança é marcada com seu impacto:"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:111
msgid ""
"*major* — affects most scripts that used the feature; you will need to port "
"code."
msgstr ""
"*major* — afeta a maioria dos scripts que usaram o recurso; você precisará "
"portar o código."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:113
msgid "*minor* — narrow API; only affects scripts that used it."
msgstr "*minor* — API restrita; afeta apenas scripts que a usaram."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:114
msgid "*behavior* — same API, different results; re-check tuned scripts."
msgstr ""
"*behavior* — mesma API, resultados diferentes; reavalie scripts ajustados."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:116
msgid ""
"Changes are grouped by impact in that order. If you just want to port your "
"code, jump to the :ref:`migration checklist <v3_9_0_migration>` at the end. "
"Each commit hash links to its diff on GitHub."
msgstr ""
"As mudanças são agrupadas por impacto nessa ordem. Se você só quer portar "
"seu código, vá direto para o :ref:`checklist de migração <v3_9_0_migration>`"
" no final. Cada hash de commit possui um link para o seu diff no GitHub."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:123
msgid "CMSIS-NN ``nn`` module removed *(major)*"
msgstr "Módulo CMSIS-NN ``nn`` removido *(major)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:125
msgid ""
"The CMSIS-NN ``nn`` module was removed, including ``nn.load()``, "
"``net.forward()``, ``net.search()``, and the ``nn_class`` helper. Model "
"inference moves to the TensorFlow Lite (``tf``) module. Scripts that loaded "
"``.network`` models with ``nn`` must be ported to ``tf`` with a TensorFlow "
"Lite model."
msgstr ""
"O módulo CMSIS-NN ``nn`` foi removido, incluindo ``nn.load()``\\ , "
"``net.forward()``\\ , ``net.search()`` e o auxiliar ``nn_class``\\ . A "
"inferência de modelos passa para o módulo TensorFlow Lite (\\ ``tf``\\ ). "
"Scripts que carregavam modelos ``.network`` com ``nn`` devem ser portados "
"para ``tf`` com um modelo TensorFlow Lite."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:131
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `fbc767b36 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/fbc767b36>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits:* `fbc767b36 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/fbc767b36>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:136
msgid ""
"``ImageReader`` / ``ImageWriter`` replaced by :class:`image.ImageIO` "
"*(major)*"
msgstr ""
"``ImageReader`` / ``ImageWriter`` substituídos por :class:`image.ImageIO` "
"*(major)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:138
msgid ""
"``image.ImageReader`` / ``image.ImageWriter`` and their ``next_frame()`` / "
"``add_frame()`` methods were removed and replaced with the new "
":class:`image.ImageIO` type, which supports both memory and file streams via"
" ``read()`` / ``write()`` / ``seek()`` / ``size()`` / ``close()``. Code "
"using the old reader/writer classes must be ported to :class:`image.ImageIO`"
" (see the renamed ``imageio_read.py`` / ``imageio_write.py`` examples)."
msgstr ""
"``image.ImageReader`` / ``image.ImageWriter`` e seus métodos "
"``next_frame()`` / ``add_frame()`` foram removidos e substituídos pelo novo "
"tipo :class:`image.ImageIO`\\ , que suporta tanto streams de memória quanto "
"de arquivo via ``read()`` / ``write()`` / ``seek()`` / ``size()`` / "
"``close()``\\ . Código que usa as antigas classes reader/writer deve ser "
"portado para :class:`image.ImageIO` (veja os exemplos renomeados "
"``imageio_read.py`` / ``imageio_write.py``\\ )."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:145
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `783a78754 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/783a78754>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits:* `783a78754 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/783a78754>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:150
msgid ":func:`fir.draw_ir` ``scale`` keyword removed *(minor)*"
msgstr "Palavra-chave ``scale`` de :func:`fir.draw_ir` removida *(minor)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:152
msgid ""
":func:`fir.draw_ir` was rewritten on top of the new image drawing pipeline. "
"The ``scale=(min, max)`` keyword was removed, and ``hint``, ``x_scale``, "
"``y_scale``, ``roi``, and positional x/y offset arguments were added. "
"Scripts that passed ``scale=(min, max)`` to :func:`fir.draw_ir` must drop it"
" and use the new arguments."
msgstr ""
":func:`fir.draw_ir` foi reescrita sobre o novo pipeline de desenho de "
"imagem. A palavra-chave ``scale=(min, max)`` foi removida, e foram "
"adicionados ``hint``\\ , ``x_scale``\\ , ``y_scale``\\ , ``roi`` e "
"argumentos posicionais de deslocamento x/y. Scripts que passavam "
"``scale=(min, max)`` para :func:`fir.draw_ir` devem removê-la e usar os "
"novos argumentos."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:158
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `0a29103b1 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/0a29103b1>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits:* `0a29103b1 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/0a29103b1>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:163
msgid "``find_lines()`` approximation *(behavior)*"
msgstr "Aproximação de ``find_lines()`` *(behavior)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:165
msgid ""
"``image.find_lines()`` now approximates gradient magnitude as ``(abs(gx) + "
"abs(gy)) / 2`` and skips magnitudes below 126. This is faster but changes "
"the set of detected lines and accumulator values, so re-check and re-tune "
"``threshold`` / ``theta_margin`` / ``rho_margin``."
msgstr ""
"``image.find_lines()`` agora aproxima a magnitude do gradiente como "
"``(abs(gx) + abs(gy)) / 2`` e ignora magnitudes abaixo de 126. Isso é mais "
"rápido, mas altera o conjunto de linhas detectadas e os valores do "
"acumulador, então reavalie e reajuste ``threshold`` / ``theta_margin`` / "
"``rho_margin``\\ ."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:170
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `902ae3c98 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/902ae3c98>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits:* `902ae3c98 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/902ae3c98>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:175
msgid ":func:`fir.snapshot` reworked *(behavior)*"
msgstr ":func:`fir.snapshot` reformulada *(behavior)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:177
msgid ""
":func:`fir.snapshot` was substantially reworked with a new keyword API "
"(``hmirror``, ``vflip``, ``transpose``, ``x_scale``, ``y_scale``, "
"``x_size``, ``y_size``, ``scale``, ``rgb_channel``, ``alpha``, "
"``color_palette``, ``hint``, ``pixformat``, ``copy_to_fb``), and the bundled"
" examples were rewritten. The previous positional/``pixformat``-only "
"behavior changed; port FIR scripts to the new keyword form (see the updated "
"thermopile-shield examples)."
msgstr ""
":func:`fir.snapshot` foi substancialmente reformulada com uma nova API de "
"palavras-chave (\\ ``hmirror``\\ , ``vflip``\\ , ``transpose``\\ , "
"``x_scale``\\ , ``y_scale``\\ , ``x_size``\\ , ``y_size``\\ , ``scale``\\ , "
"``rgb_channel``\\ , ``alpha``\\ , ``color_palette``\\ , ``hint``\\ , "
"``pixformat``\\ , ``copy_to_fb``\\ ), e os exemplos incluídos foram "
"reescritos. O comportamento anterior posicional/somente-\\ ``pixformat`` "
"mudou; porte os scripts FIR para a nova forma de palavras-chave (veja os "
"exemplos atualizados do shield termopilha)."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:185
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `53f2248b8 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/53f2248b8>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commits:* `53f2248b8 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/53f2248b8>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:190
msgid ":func:`fir.init` raises on failure *(behavior)*"
msgstr ":func:`fir.init` lança exceção em falha *(behavior)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:192
msgid ""
":func:`fir.init` now raises (and cleanly de-inits) when the thermal sensor "
"is not detected, instead of silently continuing. Wrap :func:`fir.init` in "
"``try`` / ``except`` (or ensure the sensor is connected) where you "
"previously relied on it not raising."
msgstr ""
":func:`fir.init` agora lança uma exceção (e desinicializa de forma limpa) "
"quando o sensor térmico não é detectado, em vez de continuar "
"silenciosamente. Envolva :func:`fir.init` em ``try`` / ``except`` (ou "
"garanta que o sensor esteja conectado) onde você antes dependia de ela não "
"lançar exceção."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.9.0.rst:197
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `4b2f972f3 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/4b2f972f3>`__"
msgstr ""
